{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith","id":1472377,"title":"An idea: a living Risen / Wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-13T11:35:01-08:00","id":1472377,"title":"An idea: a living Risen / Wraith","content":"I was thinking...<br /> <br /> a Risen is a Wraith who manages to develope enough mastery to reanimate and re-possess his own corpse, after dealing some kind of deal with his shadow self.<br /> Could it be done with a still living body?<br /> <br /> The basic idea is that, mixing technology and mysticism:<br /> <br /> 1- develope a numina / hedge magic spell / sorcerous ritual that allows the soul to leave behind the body: basically, to &quot;die&quot; leaving the body intact and still living ( at a cellular level ) AND / OR a drug that allows something similars ( like the film Flatliners )<br /> <br /> 2- have the body kept alive by artificial means ( life support machines, massages and treatments to avoid decubitus, intravenous nutrition ) AND / OR magic ( rituals, amulets, stasis magic or something )<br /> <br /> 3- do what Risen usually do ( learn the necessary Numinas, strike a deal with the shadow-self, return to the skinlands )<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Another idea.<br /> <br /> Could a comatose mortal develope a spectral self similar to a ghost?<br /> <br /> Could a mortal do that deliberately, leaving the body through meditation AND / OR specific drugs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T12:13:56-08:00","id":1472380,"title":"","content":"Are you familiar with Orpheus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T12:32:44-08:00","id":1472381,"title":"","content":"Those second two questions are definitely the stuff of Orpheus.<br /> <br /> For the first, I suppose it is possible given the right story, but it is such a different thing I would approach it whole cloth rather than trying to adapt the Risen. Knowing enough about the Shadow and the Risen to try this involves a lot of esoteric knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T12:48:42-08:00","id":1472382,"title":"","content":"What is Orpheus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T12:51:02-08:00","id":1472383,"title":"","content":"Even the latter part of the first question (developing a drug that allows projecting) is the stuff of Orpheus. As for the first part of the first question, one of the ghost hunter groups has exactly such a ritual: the Benadante.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T12:57:26-08:00","id":1472384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1472382#post1472382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is Orpheus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Orpheus is a corporation that specializes in techniques for interacting with the dead. Its agents include two kinds of Projectors: Sleepers (think \u201cFlatliners\u201d) and Skimmers (people capable of projecting their ghost-forms through meditation and/or drugs), as well as ghosts. Orpheus was originally a separate gameline that came out four years after Wraith ended; but Wr20 includes an appendix allowing you to approximate it in Wraith terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-13-2022, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T20:15:23-08:00","id":1472543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1472384#post1472384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Orpheus was originally a separate gameline that came out four years after Wraith ended;</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of. It is also what they gave as Wraith Revised because Wraith had some bad rep baggage even compared to other lines.<br /> <br /> But it is basically a short gameline that took off from the 6th Maelstrom to develop Wraith's lore into Revised and towards Time of Judgement.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise, yes, that's the go-to for the answers to the questions asked. Pretty on-spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T20:23:16-08:00","id":1472546,"title":"","content":"More of a sequel than a revised edition; but yes. Which is why it got an Appendix in Wr20 addressing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T07:22:29-08:00","id":1472664,"title":"","content":"It got an appendix which ported over the surface level idea. It really didn't port over anything deeper because that was pretty much impossible. Orpheus was a game with completely different themes, rules, and metaphysics and they don't translate well to Wraith. <br /> <br /> The idea of projectors does, though, which is all we need for the purposes of this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T02:31:35-08:00","id":1473810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith#post1472377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking...<br /> <br /> a Risen is a Wraith who manages to develope enough mastery to reanimate and re-possess his own corpse, after dealing some kind of deal with his shadow self.<br /> Could it be done with a still living body?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly I had a similar situation in my recent Wraith campaign. The NPCs used a ritual similar to the Soul Stealing power from the Bone Path of Necromancy but with a permanent duration, the body was kept healthy by feeding it vampire blood, which meant that the Wraith PC had their living body as one of their fetters. Theoretically said PC could have concentrated on reclaiming their body and become Risen. Instead they decided to wreak vengeance on the perpetrators.<br /> <br /> Of course it's important to bear in mind that this was me fudging the rules a bit to make an interesting story, there's no 'official' way to do this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T04:12:54-07:00","id":1478942,"title":"","content":"While sound in theory and there's enough mechanics in WtO20 to make it feasible... Why? I'm genuinely asking.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure a Living version of a risen would be heavily nerfed compared to the real thing.<br /> <br /> Since you aren't a corpse, at minimum you'd lose the abilities to soak lethal, take half-damage from bashing and treat bullets as bashing.<br /> <br /> There's also a strong argument to be had that you wouldn't get the risen's 10 health levels and instead would be stuck with the standard human 7. That is unfortunate for more than just health reasons because &quot;living&quot; wraiths have to deal with Vitality. Any wraith with a living body kicking around somewhere has their Max pathos capped by their Current temporary Corpus/Health(meaning you living risen has a Max pathos of 7 and that goes down any time they take damage).<br /> <br /> Finally, there's the issue with arcanoi levels. Humans can't normally manifest Arcanoi except in special edge-cases and even then they only get the standard freebee powers plus level 1 abilities. This is also consistent with how ghouls/revenants and kinfolk work.<br /> <br /> Though as a counter-argument to the above, Dhampyrs(the KotE variation) and Kinean are able to manifest Much higher level abilities. Orphean flatliners seem like they operate more closely to this level(I.E. competent enough to rival full-splat characters) than other half-splats. So saying your Living-Risen can use the standard array of risen abilities(which Are reduced compared to normal wraith abilities) is fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 04-16-2022, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T08:47:10-07:00","id":1478955,"title":"","content":"The reasons aren't mechanical; they're conceptual. Or rather, they're grounded in things that don't get reflected in game mechanics. The Risen don't experience the world of the living in the same way that the living do; the fact that they're animating a corpse rather than actually living is Generally viewed as something that's unnatural and wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T09:37:53-07:00","id":1478961,"title":"","content":"Yes. Thought exercises and concept tweaking aren't meant for power play necessarily, they're meant for exploring possibilities and themes. The question is not if such a character would be viable and &quot;competitive&quot; in a regular Wraith game, it is if this concept is possible within the lore, if it is backed by the rules, and to explore on what would be the consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-16T18:06:44-07:00","id":1478993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1478955#post1478955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reasons aren't mechanical; they're conceptual. Or rather, they're grounded in things that don't get reflected in game mechanics. The Risen don't experience the world of the living in the same way that the living do; the fact that they're animating a corpse rather than actually living is Generally viewed as something that's unnatural and wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1478961#post1478961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Thought exercises and concept tweaking aren't meant for power play necessarily, they're meant for exploring possibilities and themes. The question is not if such a character would be viable and &quot;competitive&quot; in a regular Wraith game, it is if this concept is possible within the lore, if it is backed by the rules, and to explore on what would be the consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that, but honestly? I struggle to see this particular concept.<br /> <br /> For a wraith that's found the secret to living again, I'd personally just make them standard human for the same reasons I'd do the same to a vampire curing themselves. The powers being a package deal with the damnation aspects seems more in line with the setting to me.<br /> <br /> If it's for a power-hungry sorcerer or flatliner, then they'd honestly get more benefit from killing off their main body than trying to cling to life. I'd also be rather thematic in a &quot;crossing the line of no return&quot; as the character literally sacrifices their normal life just for power.<br /> <br /> If it's a government experiment for some kind of super-soldier, then the above applies again. Granted, a failed &quot;living&quot; experiment could be interesting, but I struggle to find a reason why said government would keep around a failed experiment if the cost difference between &quot;failed&quot; and &quot;successful&quot; is just the 21 cents it takes to put a bullet between the eyes.(on the other hand, they could have escaped?)<br /> <br /> Granted, my views are also likely skewed because I'm one of those mutants that prefers crossover play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T08:31:27-07:00","id":1482768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1478993#post1478993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get that, but honestly? I struggle to see this particular concept.<br /> <br /> For a wraith that's found the secret to living again, I'd personally just make them standard human for the same reasons I'd do the same to a vampire curing themselves. The powers being a package deal with the damnation aspects seems more in line with the setting to me.<br /> <br /> If it's for a power-hungry sorcerer or flatliner, then they'd honestly get more benefit from killing off their main body than trying to cling to life. I'd also be rather thematic in a &amp;quot;crossing the line of no return&amp;quot; as the character literally sacrifices their normal life just for power.<br /> <br /> If it's a government experiment for some kind of super-soldier, then the above applies again. Granted, a failed &amp;quot;living&amp;quot; experiment could be interesting, but I struggle to find a reason why said government would keep around a failed experiment if the cost difference between &amp;quot;failed&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;successful&amp;quot; is just the 21 cents it takes to put a bullet between the eyes.(on the other hand, they could have escaped?)<br /> <br /> Granted, my views are also likely skewed because I'm one of those mutants that prefers crossover play.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are a necromancer experimenting with ressurection, this is a viable experience to do. Althought this could be called (by the necro-boy) as a &quot;failure&quot;, it would be still a step.<br /> <br /> And... Why simply putting a bullet into it? Just because you have designed the last tank model, doesnt mean you'll just scrap the rest of your stock. Having a few suboptimal &quot;almost super soldiers&quot; is still useful.<br /> <br /> Also, some people may be genuine interested in helping. Maybe they wanna a functional ressurection formula to help the Restless Dead. Maybe they wanna fame. There are several reasons for not doing the super best. Particularly because that, while we on the other side of the 4th wall know this is suboptimal, doesnt mean that the &quot;virtual simulations&quot; of those characters we make in our brains do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T08:33:44-07:00","id":1482769,"title":"","content":"As to the OP's question, I would say that the result would probably or possibly be a Mummy, one of the powerful ressurrected critters of the WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T10:30:29-07:00","id":1482791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1482768#post1482768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... Why simply putting a bullet into it? Just because you have designed the last tank model, doesnt mean you'll just scrap the rest of your stock. Having a few suboptimal &quot;almost super soldiers&quot; is still useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because killing it would let you make it into a stronger creature?<br /> <br /> The main reason people don't scrap tank models is because replacing them still costs more money and there's the benefit of having a larger army even if half that army is old models, but if you could Shoot a tank and it'd magically become a new model, why Wouldn't you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1482768#post1482768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, some people may be genuine interested in helping. Maybe they wanna a functional ressurection formula to help the Restless Dead. Maybe they wanna fame. There are several reasons for not doing the super best. Particularly because that, while we on the other side of the 4th wall know this is suboptimal, doesnt mean that the &quot;virtual simulations&quot; of those characters we make in our brains do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still feel that would be better covered by having the wraith resurrected as a standard human though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T10:46:04-07:00","id":1482796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1482791#post1482791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because killing it would let you make it into a stronger creature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if the ressurected &quot;Risen&quot; turned out to be a Mummy. Which imho is what it would become. By yes, I understand your point.<br /> <br /> However, there's no garantee that this &quot;living Risen&quot; would remain... Living... As an... Undead... Risen... Yeah, this is getting weird. But you're getting what I mean... Right?<br /> <br /> As in... Probably the &quot;living Risen&quot; (Mummy?) would leave the body for real after its... second(?) death?<br /> <br /> Im getting myself lost now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T15:26:06-07:00","id":1482841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1482796#post1482796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not if the ressurected &quot;Risen&quot; turned out to be a Mummy. Which imho is what it would become. By yes, I understand your point.<br /> <br /> However, there's no garantee that this &quot;living Risen&quot; would remain... Living... As an... Undead... Risen... Yeah, this is getting weird. But you're getting what I mean... Right?<br /> <br /> As in... Probably the &quot;living Risen&quot; (Mummy?) would leave the body for real after its... second(?) death?<br /> <br /> Im getting myself lost now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mummies aren't just living risen. They're Living rizen sorcerer held together with one of the most powerful works of magic ever invented, worked by the combined efforts of an awakened mage and a vampire methusela(possibly even an Ante).<br /> <br /> You can't make one by just putting a wraith in a living body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T16:25:16-07:00","id":1482852,"title":"","content":"I would not be inclined to allow wraiths to become Projectors: I would limit Projectors to living people who have had a near-death experience, kind of like the Sin-Eaters from Chronicles of Darkness's <b>Geist</b>. Once you're dead, you don't go back to living. <br /> <br /> But what Projectors let you do is to let the living more easily interact with the dead. <br /> <br /> As for why you should go with a Projector when you could have a Risen? In addition to what I stated before, there's also the fact that it's <i>much</i> easier to become a Projector than it is to become a Risen. In addition to having to go to the Underworld, get freed from your Caul, and somehow survive in wraith society long enough to learn the necessary Arcanos to attempt to Rise, you then need to bargain with your Shadow to get it to agree to the Rising. Note that you have to renegotiate every time you leave your corpse; which means that you aren't likely to leave your corpse except under extreme duress. You are <i>not</i> a reasonable replacement for a Projector, however tough you happen to be in the physical world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T04:39:03-07:00","id":1482919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1472377-an-idea-a-living-risen-wraith?p=1482852#post1482852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would not be inclined to allow wraiths to become Projectors: I would limit Projectors to living people who have had a near-death experience, kind of like the Sin-Eaters from Chronicles of Darkness's <b>Geist</b>. Once you're dead, you don't go back to living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh.... What?<br /> <br /> This is kind of off topic from the discussion. We're talking about the viability of a Projector using arcanoi to &quot;possess&quot; their living body in a similar way to Risen and what said living risen would be like(my opinion being that it'd be a waste of time and energy if it Does work, because it'd just be a Risen minus some stuff)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T04:46:12-07:00","id":1482920,"title":"","content":"Agreed. A Projector doesn't get to Possess his own body; if he wants to get back into his body, all he does is <i>stop Projecting</i>. <br /> <br /> I have a feeling that we've been talking past each other here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}